{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790342643,"nonce":"Ey/k6RalrWsRPD8BCQytTAdt2gE=","title":"compute(): unmatched kernel bodies lower to a call of the undefined $Zyntax$compute","message":"translate_compute_dispatch_call (crates/compiler/src/ssa.rs) lowers every compute() body that is not the one recognised elementwise shape or a direct-yield reduce to a call of `__internal_compute_dispatch`, which ml.zyn maps to `$Zyntax$compute`. No symbol of that name is defined anywhere in the tree. So `@kernel matmul`, `conv2d`, `fused`, `attention`, `out[i] = f(x[i])`, multi-input and broadcast elementwise bodies, and a reduce whose `yield` sits inside a loop all compile to a call of a missing runtime function.\n\nKernels are a typed subset: a body the compiler cannot lower as a kernel must be a compile error that names the unsupported kernel shape, never a runtime dispatch.\n\nFound by the GPU documentation audit, 2026-09-25 (HEAD a900deba).","files":null}]}